    {
      "id": "5f836f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "See the University Catalog for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. See the Admissions website for transfer admission requirements &amp; Admissions deadlines See approved General Education courses at CSU Fullerton. See Associate Degree for Transfer. See the Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP) .",
      "contentHtml": "<blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">University Catalog</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> for the full listing of degree requirements for this major. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the Admissions website for </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/prospectivestudent/transferlocaladmissionarea.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">transfer admission requirements</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> &amp; </span><a href=\"https://admissions.fullerton.edu/deadlines/index.php\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Admissions deadlines</a></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.fullerton.edu/undergraduate/general-education/approved-courses.html#box5\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">approved General Education </a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">courses at CSU Fullerton. </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See </span><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/apply/transfer/Pages/associate-degree-for-transfer-major-and-campus-search.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Associate Degree for Transfer.</a><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\"> </span></blockquote><blockquote><span style=\"font-size: 12px;\">See the </span><a href=\"https://registrar.fullerton.edu/articulation-tc/artic-agreements/external-exams/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">Credit by Exam information (AP, IB, CLEP)</a><a href=\"https://www.calstate.edu/attend/student-services/casper/Pages/external-exam-credit.aspx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"font-size: 12px;\">.</a></blockquote>"
    },
    {
      "id": "55826f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About This Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "53826f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "(120 UNITS) The Bachelor of Arts in Dance ( Link ) is for developing artists seeking a broad and rich background in both theory and practice. The program fosters the skills, understanding and discipline of developing dance artists. Faculty teach students as individuals, taking pride in keeping classes small to provide differentiated feedback. The robust curriculum includes intensive training in modern/contemporary dance, ballet, hip-hop styles and composition classes through a lens of cultural competency, complemented by improvisation, dance history, kinesiology, pedagogy, African American concert dance history, jazz and tap. Based in Mindful Rigor, the nurturing yet rigorous environment offers dance majors many transformative experiences to develop their unique artistry, through foundational support courses, Yoga and mindful conditioning. Throughout the year, dance majors have up to seven unique performance opportunities. Graduating students leave prepared technically and creatively to pursue work in dance and related areas. Admittance into the major is by audition. The entrance audition also serves as the placement audition. Students entering the program must attend an advising session before enrolling in the major classes. Degree Requirements Dance majors are required to enroll in a daily technique class. An assessment will determine advancement to the next level or the need to repeat the course. Majors who remain in the same level after two consecutive assessments will be counseled out of the major. Students may repeat up to eight units for each level in the requirements of modern and ballet technique and up to four units in the electives of jazz and tap technique. Repeatable courses meet major requirements. All degree candidates must: Receive a “C” (2.0) or better in all course requirements. Enroll in daily technique classes. Successfully complete the fourth level of both ballet and modern dance in order to graduate. Attend yearly dance assessments. Audition and be available for casting. In addition to the requirements for the major, students must meet all other university requirements for a bachelor’s degree. Please consult the Graduation Requirements for the Bachelor’s Degree section in this catalog for complete information.",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>(120&nbsp;UNITS)</strong></p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;Bachelor&nbsp;of&nbsp;Arts&nbsp;in&nbsp;Dance&nbsp;(<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=101&amp;poid=47246&amp;returnto=15150\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)&nbsp;is&nbsp;for&nbsp;developing&nbsp;artists&nbsp;seeking&nbsp;a&nbsp;broad&nbsp;and&nbsp;rich&nbsp;background&nbsp;in&nbsp;both&nbsp;theory&nbsp;and&nbsp;practice.&nbsp;The&nbsp;program&nbsp;fosters&nbsp;the&nbsp;skills,&nbsp;understanding&nbsp;and&nbsp;discipline&nbsp;of&nbsp;developing&nbsp;dance&nbsp;artists.&nbsp;Faculty&nbsp;teach&nbsp;students&nbsp;as&nbsp;individuals,&nbsp;taking&nbsp;pride&nbsp;in&nbsp;keeping&nbsp;classes&nbsp;small&nbsp;to&nbsp;provide&nbsp;differentiated&nbsp;feedback.&nbsp;The&nbsp;robust&nbsp;curriculum&nbsp;includes&nbsp;intensive&nbsp;training&nbsp;in&nbsp;modern/contemporary&nbsp;dance,&nbsp;ballet,&nbsp;hip-hop&nbsp;styles&nbsp;and&nbsp;composition&nbsp;classes&nbsp;through&nbsp;a&nbsp;lens&nbsp;of&nbsp;cultural&nbsp;competency,&nbsp;complemented&nbsp;by&nbsp;improvisation,&nbsp;dance&nbsp;history,&nbsp;kinesiology,&nbsp;pedagogy,&nbsp;African&nbsp;American&nbsp;concert&nbsp;dance&nbsp;history,&nbsp;jazz&nbsp;and&nbsp;tap.&nbsp;Based&nbsp;in&nbsp;Mindful&nbsp;Rigor,&nbsp;the&nbsp;nurturing&nbsp;yet&nbsp;rigorous&nbsp;environment&nbsp;offers&nbsp;dance&nbsp;majors&nbsp;many&nbsp;transformative&nbsp;experiences&nbsp;to&nbsp;develop&nbsp;their&nbsp;unique&nbsp;artistry,&nbsp;through&nbsp;foundational&nbsp;support&nbsp;courses,&nbsp;Yoga&nbsp;and&nbsp;mindful&nbsp;conditioning.&nbsp;Throughout&nbsp;the&nbsp;year,&nbsp;dance&nbsp;majors&nbsp;have&nbsp;up&nbsp;to&nbsp;seven&nbsp;unique&nbsp;performance&nbsp;opportunities.&nbsp;Graduating&nbsp;students&nbsp;leave&nbsp;prepared&nbsp;technically&nbsp;and&nbsp;creatively&nbsp;to&nbsp;pursue&nbsp;work&nbsp;in&nbsp;dance&nbsp;and&nbsp;related&nbsp;areas.</p><p></p><p>Admittance&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;is&nbsp;by&nbsp;audition.&nbsp;The&nbsp;entrance&nbsp;audition&nbsp;also&nbsp;serves&nbsp;as&nbsp;the&nbsp;placement&nbsp;audition.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;entering&nbsp;the&nbsp;program&nbsp;must&nbsp;attend&nbsp;an&nbsp;advising&nbsp;session&nbsp;before&nbsp;enrolling&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;major&nbsp;classes.</p><p></p><p><strong>Degree&nbsp;Requirements</strong></p><p>Dance&nbsp;majors&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;enroll&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;daily&nbsp;technique&nbsp;class.&nbsp;An&nbsp;assessment&nbsp;will&nbsp;determine&nbsp;advancement&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;next&nbsp;level&nbsp;or&nbsp;the&nbsp;need&nbsp;to&nbsp;repeat&nbsp;the&nbsp;course.&nbsp;Majors&nbsp;who&nbsp;remain&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;same&nbsp;level&nbsp;after&nbsp;two&nbsp;consecutive&nbsp;assessments&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;counseled&nbsp;out&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;may&nbsp;repeat&nbsp;up&nbsp;to&nbsp;eight&nbsp;units&nbsp;for&nbsp;each&nbsp;level&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;of&nbsp;modern&nbsp;and&nbsp;ballet&nbsp;technique&nbsp;and&nbsp;up&nbsp;to&nbsp;four&nbsp;units&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;electives&nbsp;of&nbsp;jazz&nbsp;and&nbsp;tap&nbsp;technique.&nbsp;Repeatable&nbsp;courses&nbsp;meet&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements.</p><p></p><p>All&nbsp;degree&nbsp;candidates&nbsp;must:</p><ul><li>Receive&nbsp;a&nbsp;“C”&nbsp;(2.0)&nbsp;or&nbsp;better&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;course&nbsp;requirements.</li><li>Enroll&nbsp;in&nbsp;daily&nbsp;technique&nbsp;classes.</li><li>Successfully&nbsp;complete&nbsp;the&nbsp;fourth&nbsp;level&nbsp;of&nbsp;both&nbsp;ballet&nbsp;and&nbsp;modern&nbsp;dance&nbsp;in&nbsp;order&nbsp;to&nbsp;graduate.</li><li>Attend&nbsp;yearly&nbsp;dance&nbsp;assessments.</li><li>Audition&nbsp;and&nbsp;be&nbsp;available&nbsp;for&nbsp;casting.</li></ul><p></p><p>In&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;major,&nbsp;students&nbsp;must&nbsp;meet&nbsp;all&nbsp;other&nbsp;university&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;bachelor’s&nbsp;degree.&nbsp;Please&nbsp;consult&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.fullerton.edu/content.php?catoid=101&amp;navoid=15099\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Graduation&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Bachelor’s&nbsp;Degree</a>&nbsp;section&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;catalog&nbsp;for&nbsp;complete&nbsp;information.</p>"
    },
